ed them 494 yards to 151 and held the ball 32:57 to 27:03.","Against the closing line (Draft Kings): Lions closed as 2.5-point favorites and covered by 22.5; the total closed at 50.5 and they combined for 45, under by 5.5."],"review":[{"title":"The algo's call","body":"Logged before the start, last snapshot Nov 15, 9:26 AM ET. It had Patriots 51% and Lions 49%, projecting Patriots 25.4 – Lions 25 (50.4 total, Patriots by 0.4).\n\nFinal: Patriots 10 – Lions 35. Wrong winner: it had Patriots at 51%, and Lions (49%) won."},{"title":"How the ratings held up","body":"Patriots came in with a 5% above average attack and a 5% stingier than average defense (5-4, 23.4 scored and 23 allowed a game over 9 games), worth about 42 and 45 games of evidence. Projected to score 25.4, they scored 10 (−15.4 points, 61% under); projected to allow 25, they allowed 35 (+10 points, 40% over).\n\nLions came in with a 14% above average attack and a league-average defense (6-2, 27.8 scored and 23.6 allowed a game over 8 games), worth about 42 and 43 games of evidence. Projected to score 25, they scored 35 (+10 points, 40% over); projected to allow 25.4, they allowed 10 (−15.4 points, 61% under).\n\nThe bigger miss was Patriots' scoring (-15.4 points against projection)."},{"title":"Where the result sat in the simulations","body":"Total: 45 against 50.4 projected (-5.4), about the 34th percentile of the simulated totals (a typical game swings ±13.2).\n\nMargin: Lions by 25 against Patriots by 0.4 projected, about the 98th percentile of the simulated margins (typical swing ±12.8).\n\nAn unusual result, but one the simulations saw regularly (roughly one game in six to one in twenty)."},{"title":"Situational factors, checked","body":"Nothing situational moved this projection (rest, travel, form and conditions were all normal), so it came down to team strength."},{"title":"Against the market","body":"DET ML (-148) at -148: the algo gave it 56% vs 57% fair (-0.8 pts) — won (+0.7u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 57%). NE ML (+124) at +124: the algo gave it 44% vs 43% fair (+0.8 pts) — lost (-1u); lost to the close (closing fair chance 43%). DET -2.5 (-120) at -120: the algo gave it 51% vs 52% fair (-0.8 pts) — won (+0.8u); same number as the close. NE +2.5 (+100) at +100: the algo gave it 49% vs 48% fair (+0.8 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. OVER 50.5 (-115) at -115: the algo gave it 51% vs 51% fair (-0.1 pts) — lost (-1u); same number as the close. UNDER 50.5 (-105) at -105: the algo gave it 49% vs 49% fair (+0.1 pts) — won (+1u); same number as the close.\n\nThe line barely moved between the algo's snapshot and the close.\n\nNo bet: nothing cleared the algo's bar before the game."},{"title":"Where the public and the money were","body":"Splits (Action Network): spread: 47% of bets on Patriots, 42% of the money — Lions covered; total: 15% of bets on the over, 17% of the money — it went under; moneyline: 17% of bets on Patriots, 12% of the money.\n\nThe sharp side by the algo's read was Lions, who won and covered."},{"title":"What the algo learns","body":"This game's own lesson: scoring came in at ×0.893 of the raw projection. It counts toward NFL scoring level, home edge and both teams' attack and defense corrections.\n\nNFL learning switches on at 20 graded games (17 so far)."},{"title":"Bottom line","body":"Wrong side, total within its normal range, margin outside its normal range (off by 25.4 points), no bet."}],"archived":"2026-11-15T17:40:24.504Z"}}}